:question
$()We have a differentiable function 
!insmath f
$(),	with values and derivatives shown in the following table.	<table class="wimscenter wimsborder">	<tr><th>
!insmath x
$()</th><th>-2</th><th>-1</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th></tr>	<tr><th>
!insmath f(x)
$()</th>	<td>$val7</td><td>$val8</td><td>$val9</td><td>$val10</td><td>$val11</td></tr>	<tr><th>
!insmath f '(x)
$()</th>	<td>$val12</td><td>$val13</td><td>$val14</td><td>$val15</td><td>$val16</td></tr>	</table>	Let 
!insmath h
$() defined by 
!insmath h(x) = $val35 f(x)
$(). Compute the derivative	
!insmath h'($val22)
$().	
$()
!exit

:hint
$()First compute the value and derivative of the function $val35 at the	point 
!insmath  x_0=$val22
$(), then apply the formula of multiplication.
$()
!exit

:help
$()
$()
!exit

:solution
$()Let 
!insmath g(x)=$val35
$(). We have 
!insmath g($val22)=$val33
$(),	
!insmath g'($val22)=$val36
$(), hence	<div class="wimscenter">	 
!insmath h'($val22) = f($val22)g'($val22) + f '($val22)g($val22) = ($val23)($val36) + ($val24)($val33) = $val37.
$()	</div>	
$()
!exit

